  "judgement": {
    "text": "We assess that spillover risk is steady, with the ladder at rung 3 because of stray drones and debris from Russian strikes near NATO's eastern borders. No new incident was reported in Europe overnight. The pattern this month is consistent with spillover from strikes on western Ukraine and the Danube ports rather than deliberate probing: the drones flew on strike headings and none loitered over allied territory.\n\nRussia's covert campaign continues at about its usual pace. Sabotage and undersea incidents remain near their baselines, and officials have not reported new arrests in the window. The sanctions talks are a cohesion problem for the EU rather than a spillover driver, although delays keep shadow-fleet tankers trading in the Baltic for longer.\n\nWe keep the 30-day odds of a deadly or deliberate incident at highly unlikely (10%). Strategic indicators remain dormant: there is no sign of Russian units moving toward Finland or the Baltic states, and no change in nuclear posture.",
    "change_my_mind": "Drones crossing on headings toward Polish military sites, or a Russian statement naming Poland's air defences as a target, would make us treat the incursions as deliberate.",
    "competing_explanations": []
  },
